  "assessment": "The change directly addresses the identified defect where password length was measured by UTF-8 byte size rather than character count. The fix replaces `len(password.encode(\"utf-8\"))` with `len(password)`, which correctly counts Unicode code points (characters) in Python 3. This aligns with the security review finding that non-ASCII characters were inflating the length metric and allows shorter visual strings to be rejected if they fall below `MIN_LENGTH`. The change is scoped only to `pwpolicy/policy.py`, preserving file shapes, data files, and constants as required.",
